{
  "id": "reviews-same-card-offline",
  "title": "Two devices review the same card offline",
  "covers": [
    "spec: Reviews never conflict; all kept, replayed in timestamp order",
    "replay: out-of-order arrival forces a full replay"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Card C exists everywhere. Phone A (offline) reviews it at T+10 and T+30. Phone B (offline) reviews it at T+20 and drills it at T+25.",
    "A syncs first: the server folds A's two reviews into C's cache; last_review_id = A's T+30 review.",
    "B syncs: its T+20 review sorts BEFORE the cached last review, so the server (and later A, when it pulls) must replay C from scratch.",
    "Every replica ends with all four rows; the replay set is ordered by (hlc, id): A@10, B@20, A@30. The drill is logged but not in the replay set."
  ],
